    orion "Potential difference. Define it."

    mc "Work done per unit charge to move a positive test charge from one point to another."

    orion "Against or along the field?"

    mc "Against."

    orion "Why does that matter?"

    mc "Because work done {i}along{/i} the field is done by the field, not on it."
    mc "The sign flips. The physics changes."

    narrator "He writes something."
    narrator "You've stopped trying to read it upside down."
    narrator "You've started watching his hand instead."
    narrator "You stop doing that too."

    orion "Equipotential surfaces."

    mc "Surfaces where every point has the same potential."
    mc "No work is done moving a charge along them."
    mc "They're always perpendicular to field lines."

    orion "Why perpendicular?"

    mc "Because if they weren't, there'd be a component of force along the surface."
    mc "Which means work would be done."
    mc "Which contradicts the definition."

    orion "Good."

    narrator "You look up."
    narrator "He said it like it cost him nothing."
    narrator "Like it was just a word."

    thought "He's never said that before."
